Author: aean0x <3682177+aean0x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 31 19:46:25 2026 +0000

    fix(state): persist system prompt text in sessions row; stop deleting just-stored prompts
    
    FA-024: 'Stored system prompt for session X is null; rebuilding from
    scratch this turn. Prefix cache will miss until the rebuild persists'
    fired 296x across sessions since 08-12.
    
    Root causes:
    1. _insert_session_row hard-coded NULL for the system_prompt column even
       when a prompt was passed — the restore path depends entirely on the
       separate system_prompts hash table + JOIN.
    2. update_system_prompt stored only the hash and NULLed the column.
    3. _delete_unreferenced_system_prompts deleted a just-stored prompt row
       when the referencing UPDATE affected 0 rows (first turn: the session
       row does not exist yet), so the hash existed but the text was gone.
    
    Fix: store the prompt TEXT in the sessions.system_prompt column on
    insert and update (hash dedup table kept), backfill the column on
    ON CONFLICT for bare gateway rows, and keep the just-stored hash out of
    the same-transaction orphan sweep. The restore JOIN falls back to the
    column text, so a deleted hash row can no longer cause a rebuild.

